<title>UK: FT SAYS IN TALKS TO BUY DUTCH FINANCIEELE DAGBLAD.</title>
<headline>FT SAYS IN TALKS TO BUY DUTCH FINANCIEELE DAGBLAD.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Financial Times, owned by publisher Pearson , has opened talks to buy Dutch financial and business newspaper Financieele Dagblad, the British daily reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are interested. There have been a series of talks over a number of years, including recently,&quot; the Financial Times quoted its deputy chief executive, Alan Miller, as saying.</p>
<p>The negotiations are believed to have the support in principle of Financieele Dagblad's owners, the Sijthoff family, and the Dutch paper's supervisory board, the FT said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
